WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:04.830
Speaker 1: To shift gears a little bit before
we get back to covid stuff, as we discussed

00:00:04.830 --> 00:00:09.760
many times during the presidency of Donald
Trump, the humiliating and cartoonish nature

00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:15.209
of Trump led to many of our historical allies
being distanced from the United States, Canada,

00:00:15.209 --> 00:00:17.290
France, Germany, others.

00:00:17.290 --> 00:00:22.800
The U.S. was increasingly not a part of major
global discussions on important issues.

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:24.670
Climate, of course, being one of them.

00:00:24.670 --> 00:00:29.810
Why on earth would a Trump led United States
be part of climate discussions when Trump

00:00:29.810 --> 00:00:33.660
said climate change was a hoax created by
the Chinese allies?

00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:35.000
Talk to each other.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:39.829
But they increasingly did not involve Trump
and the United States and the reputation of

00:00:39.829 --> 00:00:44.260
the US was in the toilet, a toilet that Trump
was flushing 10 to 15 times.

00:00:44.260 --> 00:00:47.050
Remember that our reputation was in the toilet.

00:00:47.050 --> 00:00:52.239
And exactly as predicted, the reputation of
the US is coming back quite quickly.

00:00:52.239 --> 00:00:55.720
I got a lot of phone calls during the transition
period from Trump to Biden saying, do you

00:00:55.720 --> 00:00:57.710
think we will recover our reputation quickly?

00:00:57.710 --> 00:01:03.999
And I said, I think we will, because much
of the world is eager for a non cartoonish

00:01:03.999 --> 00:01:04.999
president.

00:01:04.999 --> 00:01:09.710
And the US popularity has improved significantly
in several countries since Joe Biden took

00:01:09.710 --> 00:01:10.710
office.

00:01:10.710 --> 00:01:12.799
This is data from the latest Morning Consult
poll.

00:01:12.799 --> 00:01:19.730
Looking at the list of countries, our standing
abroad has increased dramatically in Germany,

00:01:19.730 --> 00:01:23.640
where our favorability has almost doubled
from twenty four to forty six percent.

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:29.060
Germany has followed by Japan and France,
where our favorability has gone from 36 to

00:01:29.060 --> 00:01:32.100
55 and twenty nine to forty six respectively.

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:35.740
Now to be clear, these are not exactly stellar
numbers.

00:01:35.740 --> 00:01:38.590
Despite major improvements, 37 percent of
Germans.

00:01:38.590 --> 00:01:39.869
Twenty two percent of Japanese.

00:01:39.869 --> 00:01:42.630
Twenty nine percent of French see the US negatively.

00:01:42.630 --> 00:01:48.200
Never mind other countries like Canada, 47
percent of Canadians see the United States

00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:49.200
negatively.

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:54.009
But the point is, what is happening in the
real world actually does get paid attention

00:01:54.009 --> 00:01:56.490
to and it has an impact abroad.

00:01:56.490 --> 00:02:01.119
It's not capricious negativity about the United
States.

00:02:01.119 --> 00:02:04.740
Trump out and favorability increases significantly.

00:02:04.740 --> 00:02:11.239
Now, anecdotally, Americans are also less
stressed day to day because the president,

00:02:11.239 --> 00:02:17.330
the former president, was always at risk of
making some horrifying blunder and unleashing

00:02:17.330 --> 00:02:20.340
global shame and embarrassment upon us.

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:22.379
We no longer worry about that.

00:02:22.379 --> 00:02:27.599
As important as it is to realize that our
reputation does respond very directly to who

00:02:27.599 --> 00:02:31.959
is the president and to what the president
is doing, it's also important to realize that

00:02:31.959 --> 00:02:33.920
this could happen again.

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:35.760
Most Republicans still like Trump.

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:39.420
Most Republicans still believe Trump won in
November, if you can believe that.

00:02:39.420 --> 00:02:44.799
And most Republicans would vote Trump back
today if given the chance, despite the successes

00:02:44.799 --> 00:02:50.610
of Joe Biden in his first hundred days, vaccination,
covid stimulus, rehabilitating to some degree

00:02:50.610 --> 00:02:52.890
the global reputation of the country.

00:02:52.890 --> 00:02:56.840
I'm hearing from friends and relatives in
a variety of countries, including France,

00:02:56.840 --> 00:03:00.480
Belgium, Argentina, where I was born in Israel.

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:06.310
It's primarily a feeling of relief that Trump
is gone and relief gets you part of the way,

00:03:06.310 --> 00:03:10.400
but it doesn't get you all of the way back
to a recovery in reputation.

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:16.180
Sadly, most of the world understands what
in this country nearly half of Americans don't

00:03:16.180 --> 00:03:22.480
understand, which is it's objectively bad
for us and everyone else to elect an incompetent

00:03:22.480 --> 00:03:23.840
buffoon like Donald Trump.

00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:29.180
It really shouldn't be done again, but it
might be if they get a say and if they're

00:03:29.180 --> 00:03:31.750
able to suppress the vote enough in twenty
twenty four.

00:03:31.750 --> 00:03:36.519
Remember, they didn't suppress it enough in
twenty twenty they tried, but they failed.

00:03:36.519 --> 00:03:40.989
If they succeed at voter suppression to a
greater degree in twenty twenty four, Trump

00:03:40.989 --> 00:03:42.310
could be back or someone like him.

00:03:42.310 --> 00:03:47.920
Now lastly, just because Joe Biden is restoring
our reputation to some degree.

00:03:47.920 --> 00:03:51.540
And doing good things doesn't mean bad things
don't still happen.

00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:55.719
They do, and we have to keep paying attention,
which is exactly what we're doing.

00:03:55.719 --> 00:04:01.849
In a sense, boring politics is good, but it
can lead to complacency as a result.

00:04:01.849 --> 00:04:04.829
And that is exactly how Donald Trump ended
up coming to power.

00:04:04.829 --> 00:04:07.150
Now, he has no shot at the Republican primary.

00:04:07.150 --> 00:04:09.140
Oh, he won the Republican primary.

00:04:09.140 --> 00:04:10.950
Well, there's no way that he can beat Hillary.

00:04:10.950 --> 00:04:16.590
I don't even know if I'll vote because it's
just not going to be necessary to defeat Donald

00:04:16.590 --> 00:04:17.590
Trump.

00:04:17.590 --> 00:04:18.590
Oh, Trump beat Hillary.

00:04:18.590 --> 00:04:26.400
Well, then what boring should not mean we
don't pay attention, but it's OK for it to

00:04:26.400 --> 00:04:31.650
mean less constant stress about which writes,
is the president trying to take away from

00:04:31.650 --> 00:04:34.290
people or media or from whomever?

00:04:34.290 --> 00:04:39.880
We are going to continue following the reputation
of the United States around the world, much

00:04:39.880 --> 00:04:45.520
improved in many countries, but nowhere near
where we should want to be.

00:04:45.520 --> 00:04:46.820
Let me know your thoughts.

00:04:46.820 --> 00:04:50.360
You can find me on Twitter at David Pakman.

00:04:50.360 --> 00:04:53.240
And boy, do we have a good show for you today.

00:04:53.240 --> 00:04:58.630
I think we should actually record and keep
today's show, which is not what we always

00:04:58.630 --> 00:04:59.470
do, because today's is actually a pretty good
one.

